This work-only candidate implements VS Code 1.140.0 `Position`, `Range` and `Selection` API value classes. It implements all 30 direct documented declaration entries, their six nested option fields and the 12 inherited Range entries on Selection. It is not installed in REA Studio.

The release identity is commit `07f806f999227108933c2e30515b26eecc1fda74`. The actual shipped `vscode.d.ts` is retained exactly; normalization from CRLF to LF equals the official commit's declaration file. `acquisition.json` binds ten official source/metadata records, the shipped declarations and the preserved prior 14-artifact original acquisition authority. `contracts.json` gives declaration and implementation SHA-256 identities and one-based source locations. Microsoft MIT notices and the full license are preserved.

`position-range-selection.mjs` is a new standalone module with no runtime imports. It provides zero-based UTF-16 coordinate values, ordered ranges, both documented constructor forms, all comparisons and numeric/object changes, intersection/union, selection anchor/active direction, and readonly public accessors. Unchanged operations retain the original's object aliases. Equal endpoint ranges swap endpoint references; empty Selection consequently reports `isReversed` true. Changed inherited Selection operations return Range where the original does. This matches observed original source behavior rather than introducing document clipping or new type validation.

Released source also exposes static structural guards/conversion, Min/Max, JSON/debug formatting and legacy ES5 call/apply helpers. These are implemented and finitely checked, but excluded from the 30-entry documented declaration count. Original noninteger/nonfinite, malformed duck-position, getter evaluation and coercion behavior is deliberately retained. TypeScript private/protected underscore fields remain ordinary writable JavaScript fields like the evaluated original source; public immutability does not mean deep freezing against arbitrary JavaScript mutation.

The oracle authenticates exact original source bytes, evaluates the complete three class bodies plus the exact ES5 helper and `illegalArgument` slice, and binds each transformed execution source. Node's pinned type stripper removes types; imports/exports and decorators are composed explicitly, and six named angle-bracket assertions are erased at recorded locations because the stripper rejects those tokens. Each successful oracle preparation uses five source library units and six VM evaluations. This is original source-assisted class evaluation, not an execution of the shipped extension-host bundle or original workbench. A separate successful smoke, one partial preparation failure and all three verification attempts are retained.

Final attempt 03 passes 9/9 groups with zero skips: 986 packets and 45,117 harness-direct action dispatches per role. Those counts include explicitly dispatched constructors/methods and grouped property probes; they are not a census of transitive constructor/getter/internal calls. The corpus includes 600 deterministic broad pairs (seed `0x317ab9d2`) and 240 separately shaped same-line/orientation held-out pairs (seed `0xb49f0271`), documented overloads, numerical/coercion boundaries, invalid constructors/options, structural helpers, aliases, UTF-16 and readonly/subclass/getter controls. All raw original/candidate observations remain exact, including failures.

Attempt 01 passes 4/9 and fails five groups because the verifier's Array.map kept original-VM array prototypes. Its 104 retained packets serialize identically. Attempt 02 passes 8/9 with 986 packets; five engine-generated getter-assignment errors differ only in the cross-realm receiver label. The observation encoder now creates verification-realm arrays, and the assertion normalizes only that receiver label for readonly-assignment TypeErrors. Raw errors remain unnormalized; explicit library errors and all other observed engine errors compare exactly. Five added post-attempt property reads verify unchanged readonly values. Both diagnoses and pre-correction source snapshots are preserved, and the candidate module stayed identical throughout all three attempts.

Run a new explicitly named attempt with `node run.mjs attempt-04` from this directory. Each run preserves before/after sources and invocation/raw observations in `.local/<attempt>` with exclusive-create output guards. Prospective bounds are 120 seconds, 256 MiB V8 old space, 8 MiB stdout, 2 MiB stderr and 64 MiB retained comparison JSON. Node test isolation is disabled so exactly one direct verification child is launched. The deadline terminates that direct child; no RSS watchdog or machine isolation is claimed. The finite inputs contain no original-spawned descendant code. Source reads, fingerprint I/O and VM/library setup are verification overhead; no benchmark, profiler or GUI run occurred.

This foundation does not load extensions, host an extension API service, connect these values to editor documents/cursors, clamp document bounds, implement coordinate-to-offset conversion, run RPC or reproduce whole-editor/workbench behavior. Arbitrary adversarial getters, proxies, recursive range-like objects, prototype monkey-patching and subclass overrides are not exhaustively tested or sandboxed. Engine error formatting, stacks, function source text, prototype cross-realm identity and every property descriptor are not accepted as universally identical. Finite source-bound acceptance of these value-class observations does not establish extension-host, full API or whole-product parity.
